# Battle Targeting System

## Core Targeting Principles [to-do]
- Implement proximity-based targeting (closest valid target)
- Apply universal targeting rules across all battalion types
- Restrict movement and targeting to network lines
- Ensure targets change only when proximity changes

## Target Selection Rules [to-do]
- Target nearest available entity (enemy battalion or node)
- Calculate distance from battalion center to target center
- Ensure targets are reachable via network lines
- Implement checks for valid target candidates

## Combat Range [to-do]
- Define attack range values for each battalion type
- Calculate attack range from battalion center to target
- Determine when battalions are in range to attack
- Stop movement when attack range reaches target

## Retargeting Logic [to-do]
- Implement retargeting when current target is destroyed
- Handle retargeting when node is captured
- Create logic for when better targets become available
- Ensure seamless transition between targets

## Combat Sequence [to-do]
- Verify target is in range before initiating attack
- Implement basic damage calculation logic
- Update health status after attacks
- Trigger appropriate visual feedback

The MVP implementation should focus on creating a reliable proximity-based targeting system that works within network line restrictions. Advanced features like complex pathfinding and special targeting rules can be added in future iterations. 